message: "If you use this software or methodology, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Sugarcane Yield Modeling: Spatial Data Fusion and Machine Learning"
abstract: >
  A two-stage pipeline for modeling sugarcane yield variability under
  irrigated conditions. The first stage (R, R-INLA) reconciles yield,
  soil, rainfall, weather and foliar diagnostic data and reconstructs
  missing soil measurements with a Bayesian conditional autoregressive
  spatial model, applying an isometric log-ratio transform to handle
  compositional granulometry fractions. The second stage (Python,
  scikit-learn / XGBoost / LightGBM / CatBoost / SHAP) benchmarks
  supervised regression models on the fused dataset and interprets them
  with SHAP values and partial dependence analysis, separately for
  gravity-irrigated and drip-irrigated parcels.
